WEBVTT

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.640
I'm not so fundamentally enthusiastic

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.380
Even I will participate in this

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.150
It's been a long time since we went for a drive

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.410
Everyone is excited

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.280
He's coming too

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.820
I may have no chance with him right now

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.560
But I'm definitely going

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:38.600
If you've got a good poker face

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.740
There will be something

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.810
Let's head to the mountains

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.780
We'll just get sunburned at the sea

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.920
Even though it's coat season

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.350
He is completely misunderstanding

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.590
What's going on?

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.560
Being this happy

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:14.430
I'm laughing so hard I might burst

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:22.980
I get choked up when I see his back

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:30.880
In the whirlpool of an endless smile

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:54.280
Look at this...

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:57.350
Why would anyone vandalize a
construction site? I don't get it.

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.680
What would you have to do, to do this
much damage to it anyway?

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.250
A crane or something?

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:02.880
You gotta be kidding me.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.010
Then, what could it be?

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.420
Hell if I know.

00:02:09.990 --> 00:02:11.490
Can we go inside?

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:15.360
Not yet! There's still a possibility
that it could collapse!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.530
Then when can I go in there?

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:19.130
Brrr, it's cold.

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:19.700
It's getting cold lately.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:21.540
A ghost, huh?
It's getting cold lately.

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:23.660
Huh? What did you say?

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:27.100
Would a woman come to a construction
site in the middle of the night?

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.510
Maybe there are ghosts, just like you said.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.980
Are you referring to that case again?

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.120
I don't think it has anything to
do with this vandalism.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.990
Will you knock it off already?

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:43.120
Honestly, are you sure you're not
possessed by some weird spirit?

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:53.360
Episode #17
The Truth

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.340
Let me go! Don't you touch me!
This is crazy, Uncle!

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.780
I found out that the book of
curses is at the school!

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:04.250
We don't have to hold onto some
imitation like Lise anymore!

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.150
The time to make a decision has come! Uncle!

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:10.850
Herve, you've been a little too impatient.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.090
What?!

00:03:12.090 --> 00:03:13.760
Stop it.

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:18.260
Uncle! Hey, wait! You're gonna regret this!

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.330
Uncle! Uncle!

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:23.920
Wait! Please save Anna! Uncle!

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.870
The moment those two books
are combined together

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.740
you'll lose all the memories you've ever had.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.580
You will not be the same people.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:40.180
And you will stay in these bodies
and never age, eternally.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:42.980
No...He's the enemy,

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.350
the enemy who's been
deceiving me all this time.

00:03:45.350 --> 00:03:47.910
I'm sure he's plotting to deceive me again.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.460
I see, so a Dolore told you that.

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.900
I know it's ridiculous to believe
what the enemy said,

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:57.960
but I just wanted to make sure.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.300
What he told you is true.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:11.050
Why? Why didn't you tell me the truth? Why?

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.820
Keeping it a secret from you was Lula's idea.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.550
It has nothing to do with me.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:16.550
Lula's?

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:21.080
I know, the sooner you find out the
truth, the less you're hurt by it.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.730
Things like "You're dead" and "Go fight"...

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:27.000
There are just too many things
that are hard to believe.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.570
"You'll lose your memories" could easily
be just another one of them.

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:34.400
It's just not realistic enough, right?

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:37.840
Time will pass before you know it,

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:40.340
and by the time you realize it
you'll be on this side.

00:04:40.340 --> 00:04:43.210
So, you're the only person who's
aware of this, correct?

00:04:43.210 --> 00:04:45.880
Then, I want you to tell them yourself.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:46.880
What?

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:50.790
I've experienced enough meetings and partings,

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.020
and I can't have special feelings
for each of them.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.520
I just can't afford to.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:05:01.460
Unfortunately, I no longer understand the
pain of losing your own memories.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.240
No one's coming, eh?

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:14.040
Hey!

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:14.380
Huh?
Hey!

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:14.840
Huh?

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:15.040
Huh?
You can go home now.

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.540
You can go home now.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.280
Oh, okay.

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:22.520
Take the leftovers with you.
It's better than letting them go waste.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.140
Thanks.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:30.060
Claire!

00:05:30.060 --> 00:05:31.630
Oh...

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:33.630
Can I talk to you for a minute?

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.330
Sure.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:36.530
What's up?

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.160
It's just that you didn't come to school, so...

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.640
Give me a break, Miss Grace!

00:05:45.570 --> 00:05:48.180
That was a joke.

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:51.480
Lots of stuff has become a
pain in the ass, I guess.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:54.420
I need to keep my part-time job to survive.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.890
But school, I think maybe I don't care anymore.

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:59.750
You don't care?

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.620
Right, I don't care.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:06.990
Would you say those words again for me,

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:08.620
after you listen to what I'm about to say?

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:15.470
So, basically we are...

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.470
I don't care.

00:06:17.470 --> 00:06:18.270
Claire...

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:18.470
I'm saying that because I promised I would!
Claire...

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:20.680
I'm saying that because I promised I would!

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:23.040
Do I look that way to you?

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:26.210
Yeah, there are a bunch of things
that I don't care about,

00:06:26.210 --> 00:06:30.490
but you know, disappearing is
a totally different thing!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:35.620
I wish I could say I don't give a damn
about that; I'd have it easier!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.090
But this is...

00:06:37.090 --> 00:06:43.900
No, it's not about having it easier
or whatever. It's different.

00:06:43.900 --> 00:06:49.340
I'm just...Damn, I don't even know how to put it.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.710
I don't know how to put it, but it's not the same.

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:53.980
This is different from me not caring!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.510
I'm sorry for asking you a weird favor,

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:59.080
but I just didn't know what to do.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.720
It doesn't feel real.

00:07:00.720 --> 00:07:03.580
I can't get any answer no matter
how hard I think about it.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:06.220
Yeah, I can't get an answer.

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:09.760
It doesn't matter if I tell you or tell the others,
I know I won't get an answer.

00:07:09.760 --> 00:07:11.860
If that's how it is, I shouldn't say
anything at all, I know.

00:07:11.860 --> 00:07:14.190
I know I should keep it to myself.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:17.430
But I relied on you, Claire.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:23.840
Because I felt like you'd tell me
"I don't care" or "That's no big deal".

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:25.970
I know that's not the case, but I still...

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:29.840
You always end up playing that role, huh?

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:31.050
What?

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.380
It happened before too.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.180
You were the only one who knew the secret.

00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:36.810
You didn't tell us anything.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:39.590
Remember I told you not to keep
a secret from us then?!

00:07:39.590 --> 00:07:40.560
Claire...

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.120
It's fine, because I was the one who said so!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.960
And you actually came to me.

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:49.920
You decided to share that with me,
so that's all right.

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.560
Thank you.

00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:57.140
What are you two doing here?

00:07:57.140 --> 00:07:59.240
No, what are you doing here, Sara?

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.740
I'm watching the house for Rose.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:03.850
I wanna help her in any way I can, you know.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.510
She's going though some tough
times right now, so...

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:06.280
What?

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:06.510
How much do you know about it?
What?

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.120
How much do you know about it?

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.890
Huh? "How much"? Most likely, I
know more than you know,

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:15.090
because I went there with her once.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:15.890
Huh?

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:17.520
You don't mean...

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.790
To see her father.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:20.290
What?

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:20.800
Her father?
What?

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:21.630
Her father?

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:25.700
Don't say much about it,
because it bothers Rose.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:26.830
Oh...

00:08:32.410 --> 00:08:34.070
Rose...

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:41.650
Hey, did you know about it, Claire?

00:08:41.650 --> 00:08:43.280
Nope.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.950
I wonder why she's never told us about it?

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:54.500
See you later.

00:08:54.500 --> 00:08:55.100
Okay, bye.
See you later.

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.290
Okay, bye.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.290
Huh?

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:11.650
Claire...

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:12.280
Huh?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:12.650
Do you wanna take this home?
Huh?

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:14.020
Do you wanna take this home?

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:17.320
I made a lunchbox, but I didn't get
to give it to him, so...

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:20.190
Oh, sure.

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:21.060
Rose...

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.120
Huh?

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:26.330
I didn't know anything. I'm sorry.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:28.630
Come on, don't apologize.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.870
There was nothing you could do because
I didn't tell you anything.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.100
That's amazing...

00:09:32.100 --> 00:09:33.400
What?

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:37.960
You can forgive your father who's left you all.

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:44.850
You know, all I cared about was what
I wanted him to do for me.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:46.150
"What you wanted him to do for you"?

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:49.650
Right, I wanted him to come home,

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:53.880
so when I left, he could take care
of Paul and Carrie.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:58.430
But that's changed ever since I met him again.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:03.030
He's been doing his best in order
to come home to us.

00:10:03.030 --> 00:10:06.130
He's been trying more than enough already.

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:11.070
So, now I just want to be with him.
I just want to be close to him.

00:10:11.070 --> 00:10:13.270
I just want my whole family to smile together.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:16.580
It's okay if it takes time.
It's okay if it's a slow process.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:20.210
I just think it would be nice if we
could be like that someday.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.980
Oh, yeah, what made you two come
all the way to my home?

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:28.490
Well, that's...

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:31.830
Since the enemy found out our
identities in last night's fight,

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.330
we figured that we might be summoned soon.

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:36.730
We just wanted to tell you to be ready.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:38.360
Okay.

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:48.840
Seriously, it's amazing.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:50.680
Yeah...

00:10:50.680 --> 00:10:52.450
I understand how you feel now.

00:10:52.450 --> 00:10:54.320
What?

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.220
We can't tell Rose.

00:10:58.350 --> 00:11:02.620
You know, for some reason, I've felt
pretty close with you guys.

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:05.960
It's a little different from friendship though.

00:11:05.960 --> 00:11:07.400
I felt the same way about you too.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:12.200
I just wonder why we've never tried to
understand each other more up until now?

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:17.040
If that hadn't happened to Lise...If she hadn't
been involved in an incident like that,

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:21.480
we would've been nothing but classmates who
passed by each other every now and then.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:25.510
The bond we share was born from what
we don't want to believe in.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.250
So...

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:26.750
It's like we were looking away from each other
So...

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.420
It's like we were looking away from each other

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:30.720
although we were standing
so close to each other.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:33.020
We're weak.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.990
We are.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:36.960
How about Rachel?

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:39.620
I don't have gas. Let's call it a day.

00:11:40.360 --> 00:11:41.420
Okay...

00:11:54.740 --> 00:11:58.680
No way! What do you mean by that?
Please explain!

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.880
That doesn't make sense!

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:04.840
Yes...Yes...Sure...

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:06.950
Emma?

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:07.690
Kate...

00:12:07.690 --> 00:12:09.120
Emma!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.830
Emma, what's wrong?

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.190
Emilio...

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.260
Huh?

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:16.630
He's nowhere to be found!
I can't get a hold of him!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.930
They even told me he's turned in
his resignation at work!

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:22.370
Oh, that's right! Kate, ask him, ask Herve!

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:26.070
Please, I'm sure he knows something! Kate!

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:30.380
I can't get a hold of him either.

00:12:30.380 --> 00:12:36.250
Why? Why didn't he tell me anything?
This is just...

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:43.020
They knew everything when they
approached me, approached Emma.

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:47.550
I won't forgive them. I hate them.
I hate them!

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:51.860
Herve...

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:11.220
Anna? You must be Anna, right?

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:18.720
Anna, where's Herve? Where's your brother?

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:24.500
I can't find him. I can't find him anywhere.
Mireille's gone too.

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:26.300
What?

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:32.100
Everyone disappears.
Everyone, everyone disappears!

00:13:32.370 --> 00:13:33.640
Mireille?

00:13:33.640 --> 00:13:37.340
Without even saying goodbye,
they just disappeared!

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:42.980
Calm down! Are you okay, Anna?

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:51.190
So you too...

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.090
What's going on?

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:55.360
I don't even know!

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:58.700
Damn! How much memory has
Lise recovered so far?

00:13:58.700 --> 00:13:59.230
Doctor! Dr. Bender!

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:00.400
Now she remembers Kate's full name
Doctor! Dr. Bender!

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:00.840
Now she remembers Kate's full name

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:01.040
and she's gradually remembering the diary.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:01.870
And she's gradually remembering the diary.
We've got a problem! Anna is...

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:02.240
We've got a problem! Anna is...

00:14:02.240 --> 00:14:03.770
I don't have time for that right now!

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:04.770
Give medicine to her!

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:05.540
We have!

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:05.810
Then it hasn't been enough!
We have!

00:14:05.810 --> 00:14:06.670
Then it hasn't been enough!

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:09.880
Give her 120cc of Ankaforil
and 80cc of Messeciltin!

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:10.240
But...

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:10.880
Just do it!
But...

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:11.950
Just do it!

00:14:11.950 --> 00:14:13.310
That's eleven people, right?

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:15.780
That's right. That means you
might have a chance too!

00:14:18.220 --> 00:14:21.520
So, basically you could be a part of it.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:22.960
That's what it says over there.

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:25.860
Hey, why did you ask Rachel to come with us?

00:14:25.860 --> 00:14:28.230
Because I didn't think she'd actually come

00:14:28.230 --> 00:14:29.730
because she hasn't hung out with us lately.

00:14:29.730 --> 00:14:32.220
That's a bad idea! I'm telling you!

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.070
Rachel, what do you wanna drink next?

00:14:36.070 --> 00:14:37.470
Hmm?

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:38.670
Beer, I guess.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:39.370
What?

00:14:39.370 --> 00:14:39.810
Just kidding.
What?

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:40.910
Just kidding.

00:14:40.910 --> 00:14:42.180
Rachel!

00:14:42.180 --> 00:14:43.140
I didn't remember that.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:45.910
It sure did! When that happened, you were like...

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:47.780
You guys look cute together!

00:14:47.780 --> 00:14:49.150
So, this is how it is, huh?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.220
What are you talking about?

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:53.090
You decided to play Little Miss Victim,
saying stuff about me and Nick,

00:14:53.090 --> 00:14:54.890
and I guess this is what it
was all about, huh?

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:57.120
Knock it off, Rachel!

00:14:58.360 --> 00:15:00.160
Here we go again.

00:15:00.160 --> 00:15:03.060
You've always wanted to have whatever I've had.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:05.670
Dresses, purses and makeup bags...

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:07.670
I guess the next item was my man, huh?

00:15:07.670 --> 00:15:10.340
Rachel! How dare you?!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.110
So, you do want him.

00:15:12.110 --> 00:15:14.210
You can have that thing.

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:16.200
If you don't mind that it's pre-owned.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:20.880
I saw that coming...

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:21.650
Hey, Amanda!

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:22.150
I don't care what you say to me,
but stop making fun of Luke!
Hey, Amanda!

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:25.220
I don't care what you say to me,
but stop making fun of Luke!

00:15:25.220 --> 00:15:28.190
What was that? Trying to be a good girl?
You creep me out!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.490
I'll repeat it as many time as you want!
Do not hurt Luke any more!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:33.730
Jeez, you're giving me chills!
What the hell are you doing?

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.300
Practicing for a play or something?

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:38.170
Cut it out. I can't deal with you!

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.790
Rachel!

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:57.380
Rachel!

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:59.050
Why is it you...

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:00.450
I'll take you home.

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:01.560
Why?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:03.860
"Why"? Because I'm worried about you.

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.930
Like I said, why would you be worried about me?

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.660
Because you're not the usual Rachel.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.860
"Usual"?

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:14.320
Right now, you're not the Rachel
I've been yearning for.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:19.170
Hey, Rachel!

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:21.200
Don't follow me.

00:16:53.470 --> 00:16:56.110
I've lost everything.

00:16:56.110 --> 00:16:59.550
But you knew this was going to happen
sooner or later, didn't you?

00:16:59.550 --> 00:17:01.280
You get hurt because you dream of things.

00:17:01.280 --> 00:17:05.690
Are you different? Can you even save Anna?

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:06.490
Yes, I can.

00:17:06.490 --> 00:17:07.760
That's what you wish!

00:17:07.760 --> 00:17:09.520
No, it's not!

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:11.960
Anna vomited blood.

00:17:14.290 --> 00:17:16.630
Then what happened? Where's Dr. Bender?

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:19.060
He's completely devoting his
time to that "Lise" girl.

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:26.000
Don't worry, I gave Anna some medicine.
She's stable right now.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.840
I know it may be just temporary, but...

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:32.110
Emilio, let me out of here!

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:34.950
Are you asking me to turn my
back on my people?

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.380
That's right! Turn your back on them!

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:40.650
I don't care what you do,
but don't you get me involved!

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:42.290
I'm not like you!

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:46.730
You're right, Emilio, you and I are different.

00:17:46.730 --> 00:17:49.160
I still haven't lost everything.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.530
I still have Anna!

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:55.940
Girlfriends or whatever are all replaceable,
but Anna isn't!

00:17:55.940 --> 00:17:58.440
Don't give me that crap!
Can you be any more self-centered...

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:01.270
If I apologize, will you help me?

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:05.480
I'm sorry. Emilio, I'm begging you,
please help me!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:08.000
I have no intention of losing Anna!

00:18:08.950 --> 00:18:10.150
Emilio!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:12.990
Hey, Emilio! Emilio!

00:18:12.990 --> 00:18:16.820
Wait! Please! Save Anna! Save Anna!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:21.960
Hey, what do you think about the
earrings from the other day?

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:24.160
Oh, yeah, they were so cute!

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.000
Good morning.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:27.270
Aren't you going in?

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:28.570
I was just...

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:30.440
Let me guess.

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:34.130
I bet you're thinking about skipping
the next class because it's math!

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:37.040
If that's the case, I'll come hang out with you.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:40.450
It's beautiful outside!
Besides I didn't do my homework.

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.020
Guess so. Let's go.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:47.250
Math is such a pain, you know.

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:50.960
You don't need to learn "X" and "Y"
to live a normal life, right?

00:18:50.960 --> 00:18:54.520
I mean, all you need to know
is adding and subtracting!

00:18:55.560 --> 00:18:57.000
You know what I was thinking?

00:18:57.000 --> 00:18:57.830
Yeah?

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:00.430
Basically, we'll forget about everything, right?

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:03.300
All the memories and this feeling that
I'm having right now...

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:05.040
You know, everything.

00:19:05.040 --> 00:19:07.840
Then maybe we don't have
to tell those two about it.

00:19:07.840 --> 00:19:11.310
Because the memories of lying and being
lied to will all disappear anyway.

00:19:11.310 --> 00:19:14.350
You're right. I guess we shouldn't tell those two.

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:15.820
Hey, wait a second!

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.720
You were just referring to us two, right?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:19.590
Oh...

00:19:19.590 --> 00:19:21.120
What were you talking about?

00:19:21.120 --> 00:19:21.960
Come on.

00:19:21.960 --> 00:19:23.920
What do you mean by "disappearing"?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:33.370
Hey, Kate! That's a lie, right?
We're already suffering enough now,

00:19:33.370 --> 00:19:35.470
but you're telling me it's going
to be even worse than now.

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:40.740
No way...Losing memories?! Kate, come on!

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:41.680
Kate!

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:43.610
It's no big deal.

00:19:43.610 --> 00:19:47.250
It works for me. In fact, I wouldn't mind
forgetting about my current life...

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:48.820
Don't put me in the same category with you!

00:19:48.820 --> 00:19:49.580
What?

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:55.320
I don't wanna forget!
To me, my current life is important!

00:19:55.320 --> 00:20:00.390
My family and my friends are all I've got.

00:20:00.390 --> 00:20:05.100
If I lost my memories of them,
I wouldn't be myself anymore!

00:20:05.100 --> 00:20:06.870
Wouldn't that be better actually?

00:20:06.870 --> 00:20:09.540
You'd be better off without that wishy-washy
annoying personality, don't you think?

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:09.770
Rachel, don't say that...

00:20:09.770 --> 00:20:11.170
I will not forgive you if you say any
more than you already have!
Rachel, don't say that...

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:12.840
I will not forgive you if you say any
more than you already have!

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.270
I won't forgive you!

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:15.110
Hey...

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:19.670
I don't want it to happen! I absolutely
don't want it to happen!

00:20:20.610 --> 00:20:22.620
I can't imagine me not being myself anymore.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:23.480
Rose!

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.820
No! I said, no!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:27.290
Rose!

00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.750
Claire...

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:34.430
Even if you go after her and stop her,
what will you say to her then?

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.500
What's her deal?

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.630
I wish I could yell and scream like her.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:39.800
Claire...

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:42.770
I wanna scream too.

00:20:43.400 --> 00:20:46.810
I'm scared, because it's scary!

00:20:46.810 --> 00:20:51.650
I wish I could cry and shout and get
everything off of my chest!

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:53.640
But I can't scream.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:56.780
Why is that?

00:20:56.780 --> 00:21:01.560
What is it that I can't see?

00:21:01.560 --> 00:21:03.350
Claire...

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:17.070
How's it going, Lise? How are you feeling?

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:21.040
Somebody! Hey, somebody!

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:24.340
Lise...Lise is gone!

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:31.420
My only love sprung from my only hate

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:33.820
Too early seen unknown, and known too late

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:38.760
Prodigious birth of love it is to me,
that I must love a loathed enemy

00:21:39.160 --> 00:21:41.600
Step by step, I lost track of time

00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:44.160
And kept on dancing when I met you

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:46.470
Without knowing the fate that lies in the stars

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:49.000
I can't stop falling in love

00:21:49.000 --> 00:21:51.570
An unfaithful moon's lacking morals

00:21:51.570 --> 00:21:53.910
Give light to my full-on desire

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:56.280
Grasping onto fate, I scream out

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:58.850
"Wherefore art thou Juliet?"

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.640
Go ahead and laugh at it

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:02.980
And call it stupid love

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:05.550
Throw it all

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:07.990
Because I'll be right there

00:22:08.660 --> 00:22:11.090
Oh, my Juliet...

00:22:11.160 --> 00:22:15.530
Tell me God, what do I do

00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:20.760
To make my wishes come true?

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:25.410
Ah! This is so painful

00:22:25.410 --> 00:22:28.240
I howl into the night sky

00:22:29.680 --> 00:22:36.380
Does everyone go to sleep

00:22:36.380 --> 00:22:39.620
Holding onto a thought like this?

00:22:39.620 --> 00:22:43.920
Ah! Open your eyes right away

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:46.760
Laugh at it if it's a joke

00:22:46.760 --> 00:22:49.190
Oh, my sweet Juliet

00:22:50.830 --> 00:22:53.300
You who's sleeping and I with no name

00:22:53.300 --> 00:22:54.800
Pelted by tragic rain

00:22:54.800 --> 00:22:56.460
Say good die

00:23:02.010 --> 00:23:06.680
The one who's about to lose her memories...

00:23:06.680 --> 00:23:09.120
The one who's trying to recover them...

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:09.250
Episode #18
Slight Hope
The one who's trying to recover them...

00:23:09.250 --> 00:23:11.590
Episode #18
Slight Hope
A girl revisits the place filled with memories.

00:23:11.590 --> 00:23:14.550
Episode #18
